> ### 4. Headless runner (`src/sim/headless.js`)
  
  `node Monitor/src/sim/headless.js <scenario.json> [--script <script.json>] [--out <transcript.json>] [--pure]`
  
  - A script is `[{ "t": 5.1, "seat": "plan", "cmd": {...} }, ...]`, applied when the sim reaches `t` (before the 
tick).
  - Runs with `dt 0.01`, no pacing, until `sim.done` or `t > deadlineDay + 5` (safety stop, reported in the 
transcript).
  - Transcript: `{ scenario, seed, snapshots: [sim.view('facilitator') at every integer t], messages: [every drained 
message with its t], result }`. Numbers rounded to 3 decimals so two runs compare byte-for-byte.
  - Ship three scripts in `test/scripts/`:
    - `stage1_noaction.json`: empty; must end with `lost: "deadline"` (pipe never cleared), finish absent.
    - `stage1_pm_play.json`: Site rides to 7+20 before Day 6; at the collapse Site stops work on zone 1, Plan commits 
`lend` (exc's machine → pipe) + `hold back 2 days`; Site rides to the excavator, finds the lend not carried out (F1), 
confirms `notDone`, Plan `radio`s it, Site confirms `done`; Site rides to the backfill crew and confirms the hold; at 
the argument Plan holds back until pipe is 2 days ahead; when the Day 17 forecast lands Plan does not rent the pump 
(push stage); Plan enters inspection numbers as zones close; nobody buys anything else. Expect: the collapse `event` 
message at `t = 5.0 ± 0.02`; `finishDay` greater than `promisedDay` (35) and less than `deadlineDay - 1`; no `lost`. 
Report the actual finish, idle days and spend in NOTES: the design doc's "36 to 38" predates the order-lag and rework 
rules and will be corrected from your numbers.
    - `stage2_pull_play.json`: huddle: `setStart back 12`, `protect trench_box 600 900`; Rules holds permits: Plan 
enters zone 1 and 2 codes at start, 3 and 4 as zones sign; Site stands at the excavator when the zone 2 and 3 
boundaries are reached (so F2 cannot fire there); same collapse handling (the box halves the clearing); Plan `pay`s 
the pump when the Day 17 forecast lands. Expect: `finishDay` less than `deadlineDay - 1`, no `lost`, `idleCrewDays` 
lower than the Stage 1 script's, `peakOpenTrenchFt` ≤ 3000 (two zones), the collapse card `cardWhenProtected`, 
`finesUsd` 0. Report the numbers in NOTES.
  
  ### 5. Golden harness (`src/sim/goldens.js`)
  
  `node Monitor/src/sim/goldens.js Data/goldens/no_events.json` runs every case in `pure` mode (build a minimal 
scenario from the case's `startDay` and `machines`, 6,000 ft, `capFt` as the WIP cap), compares `finishDay`, 
`idleDays` per crew, `crewCostUsd`, `peakOpenTrenchFt` with the tolerances in the file's `_doc`, prints one line per 
case with PASS/FAIL and the deltas, exits 0 only if all pass.
  
  ### 6. Tests (`test/sim*.test.js`)
  
  Unit tests for: order landing (Site present vs absent), `setStart` nacks, `hold` with and without `days`, F1 
behaviour and catch, permit gating and the open-zone limit nack, hold point gating, stop-work reach and mood steps, P1 
durations by size and under a box (2 → 1 day for Standard), rain rework arithmetic (1,300 ft open → 3 days; with pump 
→ 1.5) and `rainRateRestore`, conflict detection, resolution and the once-per-pair rule, `inspect` answers at a 
seepage station and at the collapse station, budget/deadline loss, determinism (two headless runs of `stage1_pm_play` 
produce identical transcripts), view filtering (Plan view has no live positions; Site view has no budget; the words 
`correct|wrong|score|well done|should have` appear in no Plan or Site view and no host-bound message; the facilitator 
view and internal ids are exempt).
  
